<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Connecticut</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Connecticut is a state in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-england">New England</a> region of the north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, named after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/connecticut-river">Connecticut River</a>. Its lands were home to Algonquian peoples such as the Pequot, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohegan">Mohegan</a> and Niantic before English colonists founded settlements in the 1630s, and the colonies of Connecticut and New Haven united in 1665. One of the original thirteen states, it ratified the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitution-of-the-united-states">US Constitution</a> in 1788.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/connecticut.jpg" alt="Connecticut" width="320" height="252" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean-Pierre Demailly, xrmap authors, Commons users (SVG) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Connecticut.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
